## Introduction

Codeforces is a platform where programmers can practice their coding skills, compete with others, and learn from different approaches to solving problems. The problems on Codeforces cover a variety of topics, from basic algorithms to advanced data structures and algorithms.

This repository serves as a collection of my solutions to the problems I have encountered on Codeforces. Each solution is accompanied by a detailed explanation of the approach and any relevant code snippets.

## Getting Started

To get started with this repository, you can clone it to your local machine using the following command:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/codeforces-solutions.git
```

Replace `your-username` with your GitHub username.

Once you have cloned the repository, you can navigate to the directory and explore the solutions. Each solution is organized in a separate directory, and the README file within each directory provides a detailed explanation of the problem and the solution.

## Contributing

Contributions to this repository are welcome! If you have solved a problem on Codeforces and would like to share your solution, please follow these steps:

1. Fork the repository.
2. Create a new branch for your solution.
3. Add your solution to the appropriate directory.
4. Write a detailed README file explaining the problem and your solution.
5. Commit your changes and push them to your fork.
6. Create a pull request to merge your changes into the main repository.

Please ensure that your code is well-documented and follows the same style and conventions as the existing solutions.

## License

This repository is licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE). You are free to use, modify, and distribute the code as long as you include the original license and attribut<|fim_suffix|>e.
