# Codeforces
This repository contains my solutions to various problems on the Codeforces platform. It includes solutions to problems from different contests and categories, showcasing my problem-solving skills and coding abilities.

## Table of Contents
- [Introduction](#introduction)
- [Getting Started](#getting-started)
- [Contributing](#contributing)
- [License](#license)

## Introduction
Codeforces is a popular online platform for competitive programming and algorithmic challenges. It offers a wide range of problems for participants to solve, covering various topics and difficulty levels. This repository serves as a collection of my solutions to these problems, providing a reference for my progress and understanding of different algorithms and techniques.

## Getting Started
To get started with this repository, you can follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository to your local machine using the following command:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/codeforces-solutions.git
   ```

2. Navigate to the cloned repository:
   ```
   cd codeforces-solutions
   ```

3. Explore the different directories and files within the repository. Each directory corresponds to a specific contest or problem, and the files within each directory contain my solutions to the respective problems.

4. Review the code and comments within the files to understand the problem-solving approaches and techniques used.

5. If you want to contribute to this repository, please refer to the [Contributing](#contributing) section for guidelines on how to do so.

## Contributing
Contributions to this repository are welcome! If you have solved a problem on Codeforces and would like to share your solution, you can follow these steps:

1. Fork the repository to your own GitHub account.

2. Clone your forked repository to your local machine:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/codeforces-solutions.git
   ```

3. Create a new branch for your solution:
   ```
   git checkout -b your-solution-branch
   ```

4. Add your solution file(s) to the appropriate directory within the repository.

5. Commit your changes with a descriptive commit message:
   ```
   git commit -m "Add solution for Problem XYZ"
   ```

6. Push your changes to your forked repository:
   ```
   git push origin your-solution-branch
   ```

7. Create a pull request from your forked repository to the main repository.

8. Provide a detailed description of your solution and any relevant information in the pull request.

9. Wait for the maintainers to review your pull request and provide feedback.

10. Make any necessary changes based on the feedback and resubmit the pull request if required.

## License
This repository is licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE). Feel free to use and modify the code as per the terms of the license.

Thank you for visiting my Codeforces solutions repository. I hope you find it helpful and informative. If you have any questions or need further assistance, please don't hesitate to reach out.

Happy coding!
