# Code Translation Challenge

Welcome to the Code Translation Challenge! In this challenge, you will be tasked with translating a given code snippet from one programming language to another. Your goal is to ensure that the translated code meets the syntax and logic requirements of the target programming language.

## Instructions

1. Read the provided code snippet in the source programming language.
2. Translate the code snippet to the target programming language.
3. Ensure that your translated code meets the syntax and logic requirements of the target programming language.
4. Validate your solution against the provided test cases to ensure its accuracy.
5. Your solution should strictly consist of the corrected code only.
6. Wrap your code using ``` to format it properly.

## Example

### Source Code (Java)

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class A {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = in.nextInt();
        int m = in.nextInt();
        if (n == 0 && m != 0)
            System.out.println("Impossible");
        else {
            int min = n + Math.max(0, m - n);
            int max = n + Math.max(0, m - 1);
            System.out.println(min + " " + max);
        }
    }
}
```

