#include <iostream>

int main() {
    int n, m;
    std::cin >> n >> m;
    if (n == 0 && m != 0)
        std::cout << "Impossible";
    else {
        int min = n + std::max(0, m - n);
        int max = n + std::max(0, m - 1);
        std::cout << min << " " << max;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

## Submission

1. Fork this repository.
2. Create a new branch for your solution.
3. Add your solution to the repository.
4. Commit your changes and push them to your forked repository.
5. Create a pull request to merge your solution into the main repository.

## Evaluation

Your solution will be evaluated based on the following criteria:
- Correctness: Your translated code should produce the same output as the original code for the provided test cases.
- Syntax: Your translated code should follow the syntax rules of the target programming language.
- Logic: Your translated code should maintain the same logic as the original code.

## Additional Resources

- [Java Documentation](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/)
- [C++ Documentation](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp)

Good luck with your code translation challenge! If you have any questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask.
